; Iter 160 — first-run tutorial prompt. Hidden by default; main.gd
; activates only when GameState.has_completed_tutorial is false AND
; we're in room 0. Bottom-center, big enough to read at a glance,
; warm-cream color matching the title family. Prompts cycle through
; MOVE → ATTACK → DASH → PICK UP, advancing on detected input.
; Starts modulate.a = 0 so the fade-in tween from main.gd has a
; clean ramp.
; Iter 171 — tutorial prompt subdued. Pre-iter-171 the 26 pt warm-
; gold "DASH — SHIFT" dominated the bottom of the screen
; (user-reported "tutorial feels a bit too in your face"). Now:
;   • Font 26 → 16 (60% smaller — readable but not commanding)
;   • Color cream (1.0, 0.92, 0.72) at full alpha → dimmer cream
;     (0.78, 0.72, 0.58) at 0.80 alpha — quiet annotation
;   • Outline 4 → 2 (subtle definition vs heavy block-outline)
; Iter 179 — back to BOTTOM-center. The top-center position from
; iter-171 placed the label at y=96..124 — INSIDE the playfield
; (room inner starts at y~60). On a fresh boot you saw "MOVE - WASD"
; floating over the floor mid-action. Bottom dead-strip (y=688..708,
; 6 px above viewport bottom, the space below the room frame) is the
; canonical "control hint" zone Hades/Isaac both use. Subtle by
; alpha + font size, but out of the play area.
